# No AI authorship

Never add any AI, agent, model, or coding tool as author, co-author, committer, or contributor. Leave no trace that an AI was involved.

## Forbidden in git, PRs, and code

- `Co-authored-by` / `Co-Authored-By` for Cursor, Claude, Copilot, ChatGPT, Gemini, Grok, Codex, or any other AI
- Trailers or headers like `Generated-by`, `Assisted-by`, `Made-with`, `Signed-off-by` pointing at an AI
- Commit messages, PR titles/bodies, comments, file headers, or docs that mention AI involvement
- `--author`, `GIT_AUTHOR_*`, or `GIT_COMMITTER_*` overrides that set an AI identity

```text
# BAD
Co-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Made with Cursor
Generated by Claude

# GOOD
Subject and body only. Human author from this repo's git identity.
Co-authored-by: SantiMerino <santimerinoh12@gmail.com>
```

## Required identity in this repo

- **Author:** `Santiago Merino <santiago@equitty.com>`
- **Human co-author** (when the user asks to include one): `SantiMerino <santimerinoh12@gmail.com>`
- Human `Co-authored-by` is allowed only for people the user names. Never for AI.
